workflow:
1. User -> Transportation Planner;
2. Transportation Planner -> Accommodation Planner;
3. Accommodation Planner -> Restaurant Planner
   Accommodation Planner -> Attractions Planner (in parallel);
4. Restaurant Planner, Attractions Planner -> Final Plan Summarizer;
5. Final Plan Summarizer -> End.

Description:
First, the Transportation Planner designs a flight-based closed-loop route using ONLY major Texas cities (Houston, Dallas, San Antonio, Austin) for the 3 stops. They proactively validate accommodation feasibility for party-compliant entire-home stays using AccommodationSearch previews, starting with the default city trio (Houston, Dallas, San Antonio). After 2 consecutive route adjustment attempts (using distinct combinations of the 4 major cities) failing accommodation validation, mandatory user escalation occurs. This pre-validated framework passes to the Accommodation Planner. Simultaneously, Restaurant and Attractions Planners curate non-repeating dining/activities matching Texas locations. The Final Plan Summarizer enforces all constraints (budget, closed loop, no repeats) before delivery.
